## Known pre-existing failure (NOT caused by this task)
`node src/scripts/check-loam-ui.mjs` fails with `8 !== 7` on the
`assert.equal(await page.locator('#homeModes button').count(), 7)` line. Verified
pre-existing: `git stash push -u` of the entire fc-09 change set and re-running the gate on
the clean tree produces the identical `8 !== 7` assertion, and the gate only counts
home-page mode buttons, a file this task does not touch. It is a stale count in the gate
itself, not a regression from fc-09.

Also noted: `@testing-library/user-event` is not installed in `packages/web`, so the panel
test uses `fireEvent` from `@testing-library/react` instead.

## Self-review after the fact (interpretations and gaps)

Re-auditing the delivered work surfaced two things worth stating plainly.

**1. The `createEffectcraftExecutor` / `createRoundTripExecutor` are not yet consumed.**
A reference search confirms `createRoundTripExecutor` and `createEffectcraftExecutor`
appear only in `packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.ts` (the definitions) and in
`packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.test.ts` (the tests). Nothing constructs a
`VideoStudioClient` anywhere in `packages/web/src` yet, so no production code path reaches
the effects executor today. The interpretation I had to guess at: the task asked for these
executors, and the panel drives its round trip directly through the two bridge refs, so I
delivered the executors as the documented seam and tested them, rather than inventing a
wiring that no caller needs yet. If the intent was that agent `target: "effects"` commands
must be executable end to end, that wiring is still missing and is the next piece.

**2. `Done` is disabled rather than explained when there is no project.** I initially
"fixed" this by making `Done` show a notice when `projectPath` was null. A test I wrote for
that branch failed and disproved the premise: `openInEffects` always sets a derived path via
`effectsProjectPathFor(clip, taskId)`, so while the effects engine is showing, `projectPath`
is never null. The branch was unreachable dead code, so I reverted both the change and the
test. Current behaviour stands as delivered: `Done` is disabled (via `!projectPath`) and the
round trip reports failures through the notice banner.

**3. `openInEffects` trusts the panel's own project path.** It derives the path from the
clip and the task id rather than requiring the effects engine to confirm it saved. This is
consistent with `planRoundTrip`, which does the same, but it means a user-edited composition
is named by Loam rather than by the engine. Left as is deliberately: the engine's own
`inspect()` result takes precedence when it reports one.

Gates re-run after the reverts: web `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, touched web suites 12/12 pass,
working tree clean.
